(26,'UT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu Assistant Public Prosecutor Recruitment 2025 – Walk in for- 01 Posts','UT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu','DL','Full-time','','UT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu Recruitment 2025 for 01 posts of Assistant Public Prosecutor. Candidates with LLB, LLM Can attend the walkin. The Walk-in on 22-09-2025. For detailed information please visit UT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu official website, ddd.gov.in\n\nApplication Fee\n\nNot Mentioned.\n\nUT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu Recruitment 2025 Important Dates\nDate of Walk in Interview: 22-09-2025, at 11:00 am.\n\nUT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu Recruitment 2025 Age Limit\n\nAge Limit: Not exceeding 50 Years\nAge relaxation is admissible as per rules\n\nQualification\n\nBachelor of Law or Master of law from recognized University\nAdvocate who is practicing as an advocate in any Civil Judge / Chief Judicial Magistrate\'s Court or any above court for last 03 years.\n\nSalary\n\n\nMonthly Consolidated Pay ₹. 18,000/- per month\n\nUT Administration of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu Recruitment 2025 Vacancy Details\n\nPost Name	Total\nAssistant Public Prosecutor\nJob vacancy notifications	01',1,'2025-09-18','2025-09-22','2025-09-20 10:17:55','https://ddd.gov.in/','https://cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in/s371e09b16e21f7b6919bbfc43f6a5b2f0/uploads/2025/09/20250917737660653.pdf',0),
(27,'District Legal Services Authority Ujjain (DLSA Ujjain) Para Legal Volunteer Recruitment 2025 Apply Offline for - 170 Posts','District Legal Services Authority Ujjain','MP','Full-time','','District Legal Services Authority Ujjain (DLSA Ujjain) Recruitment 2025 for 170 posts of Para Legal Volunteer. Candidates with 10TH Can Apply Offline. The Offline application opens on 23-09-2025, and closes on 10-10-2025. The candidate shall apply Offline through DLSA Ujjain website, ujjain.dcourts.gov.in\n\nApplication Fee\n\nNo Application Fee\nDLSA Ujjain Recruitment 2025 Important Dates\nStarting Date for Apply: 23-09-2025\nLast Date for Apply: 10-10-2025\n\nDLSA Ujjain Recruitment 2025 Age Limit\nMinimum Age Limit: 18 Years\nAge relaxation is applicable as per rules.\n\nQualification\n\nCandidates Should Posses 10TH Pass\n\nDLSA Ujjain Para Legal Volunteer Recruitment 2025 Vacancy Details\n\nPost Name	Total\n\nPara Legal Volunteer	170',170,'2025-09-23','2025-10-10','2025-09-25 10:41:16','https://cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in/s3ec0229539ed932d32f1c56324cded92c/uploads/2025/09/2025092393.pdf','https://ujjain.dcourts.gov.in/',0),
(28,'Canara Bank Apprentice Recruitment 2025 -Apply Online for -3500 Posts by Oct 12','Canara Bank','RJ','Full-time','','The Canara Bank Recruitment 2025 is out for 3500 posts of Graduate Apprentice. Candidates with Any Graduate Can Apply Online. The online application opens on 23-09-2025, and closes on 12-10-2025. The candidate shall apply online through Canara Bank website, canarabank.bank.in\n\nApplication Fee\nApplication fee/ Intimation charges for Registration for Graduate Apprentice on Bank’s portal:\n\nFor All Others: Rs. 500/- (incl. intimation charges)\nFor SC/ST/PwBD Category: NIL\n\nCanara Bank Apprentice Recruitment 2025 Important Dates\nStarting Date for Apply Online: 23-09-2025\nLast Date for Apply Online: 12-10-2025\n\nCandidates are required to register on Apprenticeship portal www.nats.education.gov.in before applying for apprenticeship training in the Bank: 22-09-2025 onwards if not registered earlier\n\nCanara Bank Apprentice Recruitment 2025 Age Limit\nMinimum Age Limit: 20 Years\nMaximum Age Limit: 28 Years\nCandidates must have been born not earlier than 01.09.1997 and not later than 01.09.2005 (both days inclusive).\n\nQualification\n\nA Degree (Graduation) in any discipline from a University recognized by the Govt. of India or any equivalent qualification recognized as such by the Central Government. Candidates must have passed their Graduation not earlier than 01.01.2022 and not later than 01.09.2025 (both days inclusive).\n\nSalary\nA monthly stipend of Rs. 15,000/- (including subsidy amount, if any, by Govt. of India) shall be paid to the apprentice during the period of apprenticeship training. The Apprentices are not eligible for any other allowances/ benefits.\nCanara Bank will make a payment of 10,500/- into the apprentices account on a monthly basis. Government share of Stipend of Rs. 4500 will be directly credited to the Apprentices Bank account through DBT mode as per extant guidelines.\nThe stipend shall be paid to Apprentices each month after adjusting Loss of pay, If any.\n\nSelection Process\n\nTest of local language\n\nCandidates who produce 10th or 12th standard mark sheet/ certificate evidencing having studied the specified opted local language will not be required to undergo the local language test.\nFor other candidates, the test for knowledge of local language will be conducted as a part of selection process. It will be conducted when the candidate is called for Document Verification by the Bank.\nCandidates who fail to qualify this test will not be engaged as apprentice.\nPhysical/ Medical fitness\n\nEngagement of selected Apprentices is subject to his/her being declared medically fit as per the requirement of the Bank.\nEligibility\n\nThe merit list of those candidates who have applied will be prepared State wise in descending order on the basis of marks/percentage obtained in 12th Std (HSC/10+2)/ Diploma Examination.\nIn case more than one candidate is having the same percentage, such candidates will be ranked according to their age in descending order in the merit.\nThe minimum qualifying marks will not be less than 60% (55% for SC / ST /PwBD candidates) 12th Std (HSC/10+2)/ Diploma Examination.\nThe fraction of percentage so arrived will be ignored i.e. 59.99% will be treated as less than 60% and 54.99% will be treated as less than 55% and will be treated as not eligible / unfit for the subject selection process.\nMerit list will be prepared based only on the information submitted by the candidate during online application. In case of any discrepancy observed at the time of Document Verification, the application will be disqualified summarily.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nCandidates have to apply online from 23.09.2025 to 12.10.2025 through the link provided in the Bank’s website www.canarabank.bank.in - Careers- Recruitment - Engagement of Graduate Apprentices in Canara Bank under Apprentices Act, 1961 for FY 2025-26 and no other mode of application will be accepted.\n\nCandidate will have to mention their enrollment ID generated after applying on NATS portal while applying for training seats.\n\nPre-Requisites for Applying Online:\n\nScan: Photograph (4.5cm × 3.5cm), Signature, Left thumb impression, Hand written declaration\nSignature in CAPITAL LETTERS will NOT be accepted\nThe photograph/ signature/ left thumb impression/ handwritten declaration/ should be properly scanned and should not be smudged/ blurred\nThe above mentioned hand written declaration has to be in the candidate’s hand writing and in English only and should NOT BE IN CAPITAL LETTERS. If it is written by anybody else or in any other language, the application will be considered as invalid.\nKeep the necessary details/documents ready to make Online Payment of the requisite application fee/ intimation charges\n\nProcedure for Applying Online:\n\nCandidates will have to click on “Click Here For New Registration” to register their application by entering their basic information in the online application form. After that a provisional registration number and password will be generated by the system and displayed on the screen\nCandidates are required to upload their photograph and signature as per the specifications given in the Guidelines for Scanning and Upload of Photograph and Signature.\nCandidates while filling their on-line application, the name of the candidate and his / her father / husband etc. should be spelt correctly in the application as it appears in the certificates / mark sheets.\nAny change / alteration found may disqualify the candidature.\nThe candidates name in the online application should be as it appears in SSC/SSLC/X Standard Marks Card.\nIn case the candidate has changed his/her name, the changed name should be as per the Gazette Notification/ Marriage Certificate.\nCandidates should fill all the fields in the on-line application.\nCandidates are advised to carefully fill in the online application themselves as no change in any of the data filled in the online application will be possible/ entertained\nPrior to submission of the online application candidates are advised to use the “SAVE AND NEXT” facility to verify the details in the online application form and modify the same if required.\nNo change is permitted after clicking on FINAL SUBMIT Button. Submission of incorrect / false information in the online application will render the candidature invalid.\n\nCanara Bank Recruitment 2025 Vacancy Details\n\nPost Name	Total\n\nGraduate Apprentice	3500',3500,'2025-09-23','2025-10-12','2025-09-25 10:45:50','https://nats.education.gov.in/','https://canarabank.bank.in/UploadedFiles/Pdf/NOTIFICATION-%20APP-22.pdf',0),
(29,'Staff Selection Commission (SSC) Delhi Police Constable Recruitment 2025 -Apply Online for 7565 Posts by- Oct 21','Staff Selection Commission (SSC)','DL','Full-time','','Staff Selection Commission (SSC) Recruitment 2025 for 7565 posts of Constable. Candidates with 12TH Can Apply Online. The online application opens on 22-09-2025, and closes on 21-10-2025. The candidate shall apply online through SSC website, ssc.gov.in\n\nApplication Fee\n\nFor all candidates: 100/- (Rupees One Hundred only)\nFor Women candidates and candidates belonging to Scheduled Castes (SC), Scheduled Tribes (ST) and Ex-servicemen (ESM): NIL\n\nSSC Recruitment 2025 Important Dates\nStarting Date for Apply Online: 22-09-2025\nLast Date for Apply Online: 21-10-2025\nLast date and time for making online fee payment: 22-10-2025\nDates of ‘Window for Online Application Form Correction’ and online payment of Correction Charges: 29-10-2025 to 31-10-2025\nTentative Schedule of Computer-Based Examination: December, 2025/ January, 2026\n\nSSC Recruitment 2025 Age Limit (as on 01-07-2025)\nMinimum Age Limit: 18 Years\nMaximum Age limit: 25 Years\nCandidates should not have been born earlier than 02-07-2000 and later than 01-07-2007\n\nQualification\n\n10+2 (Senior Secondary) passed from a recognized Board. Educational qualification is relaxable up to 11th passed for the:\nSons/ daughters of serving, retired or deceased Delhi Police Personnel/ Multi-Tasking Staff of Delhi Police, and\nBandsmen, buglers, mounted constables, drivers, dispatch riders, etc. of Delhi Police only.\n\nSalary\n\nPay Scale: Pay Level-3 (₹ 21700- 69100/-) (Group ‘C’,)\nSSC Constable Recruitment 2025 Vacancy Details\nPost Name	Total\n\nConstable (Exe.)-Male	4408\nConstable (Exe.)-Male [Ex-Servicemen (Others)]Anganwadi recruitment notifications	285\nConstable (Exe.)-Male [Ex-Servicemen (Commando)]	376\nConstable (Exe.)-Female	2496',7565,'2025-09-24','2025-10-21','2025-09-25 10:50:56','https://ssc.gov.in/api/attachment/uploads/masterData/NoticeBoards/Notice_of_DPCE_2025.pdf','https://ssc.gov.in/api/attachment/uploads/masterData/NoticeBoards/Notice_of_DPCE_2025.pdf',0),
(30,'Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Section Controller Recruitment 2025 - Apply Online for 368 Posts by Oct 14','Railway Recruitment Board (RRB)','AP','Full-time','','Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Recruitment 2025 for 368 posts of Section Controller. Candidates with Any Graduate Can Apply Online. The online application opens on 15-09-2025, and closes on 14-10-2025. The candidate shall apply online through RRB website, rrbahmedabad.gov.in.',368,'2025-09-15','2025-10-14','2025-09-29 11:25:14','https://www.rrbapply.gov.in/#/auth/landing','https://www.rrbchennai.gov.in/downloads/CEN-04-2025-Section-Controller-08-09-2025.pdf',0),
(31,'Haryana Power Utilities Assistant Engineer Recruitment 2025 - Apply Online for 285 Posts','Haryana Power Utilities','HR','Full-time','','Haryana Power Utilities has released an official notification for the recruitment of 285 Assistant Engineer Posts. Interested and eligible candidates can apply Online through the official Haryana Power Utilities website. The last date to submit the application form is 29-10-2025. In this article, you’ll find the Haryana Power Utilities Assistant Engineer Posts recruitment details, including eligibility criteria, age limit, salary structure, selection process, application steps, and direct links to the official notification and Online application form\n\n\nCompany Name	Haryana Power Utilities\nPost Name	Assistant Engineer\nNo of Posts	285\nSalary	Rs. 53100-167800\nQualification	B.Tech/B.E, M.E/ M.Tech\nStart Date for Online Apply	29 September 2025\nLast Date for Online Apply	29 October 2025\nOfficial Website	dhbvn.org.in\nHaryana Power Utilities Assistant Engineer Vacancy Details\nPost Name	Name of Utility	Total\n\nAssistant Engineer (Electrical Cadre)	HVPNL	22\n\nHPGCL	83\nUHBVNL	52\n\nDHBVNL	54\nAssistant Engineer (Mechanical Cadre)	HPGCL	55\nAssistant Engineer (Civil Cadre)	HVPNL	07\n\nHPGCL	08\nUHBVNL	02\n\nDHBVNL	02\nAge Limit (as on 29-10-2025)\nMinimum Age Limit: 20 Years\nMaximum Age limit: 42 Years\nThe relaxation in age limit is admissible to candidates of Haryana Domicile only.\nUpper age limit is relaxable as admissible under rules/registrations/instructions of HPUs/ Haryana Government\nApplication Fee\nFor Male candidates of SC (DSC/ OSC)/ BC-A (NCL)/ BC-B (NCL)/ ESM/ EWS categories of Haryana only.: Rs.148/-\nFor Female candidates of all (General and Reserved) categories of all States: Rs.148/-\nFor Male Candidates of General Category including Dependent Son of Ex-Servicemen of Haryana, For Male Candidates of all reserved categories of other States, All remainingCandidates: Rs.590/-\nFor all Persons with Disabilities (Candidates of Haryana only): NIL\nThe application feesisto be paid onlinethrough electronicmode i.e. Debitcard/ Credit card/ Netbanking.\nFees once paid is neithertransferable norrefundable / adjustable\nNo concession of fee is admissible to candidates belonging to States other than Haryana\nImportant Dates\nStarting Date for Apply Online: 29-09-2025 (10:00 Hrs) (Monday)\nClosing Date for Apply Online: 29-10-2025 (23:59 Hrs) (Wednesday)\nCut-offdate forthe purpose of UpperAge Limit/Reservation/ Essential Qualification etc.: 29-10-2025 (Wednesday)\nEligibility Criteria\nFull-Time Bachelor of Engineering Degree or equivalent Degree from a University duly recognized by Central Government or a State Government with a minimum 60% marks in respect of General category/ other category candidates and 55% marksin respect of SC category candidates of Haryana domicile\nFull-time Master of Engineering Degree or equivalent Degree from a University duly recognized by Central Government or a State Government with a minimum 60% marks in respect of General category/ other category candidates and 55% marks in respect of SC category candidates of Haryana domicile, in the Electrical/ Electrical & Electronics Engineering disciplines,\nIn case of candidate having full time Bachelor of Engineering Degree or equivalent Degree in Electrical/ Electrical & Electronics Engineering with marks less than 60% for General/Other candidates & lessthan 55% for SC category candidates of Haryana domicile.\nMust have passed Hindi/ Sanskrit upto matric standard or in Higher Education.\nSelection Process\nThe candidates who have acquired the essential qualification asmentioned at above and must have qualified the Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering (GATE2022/ GATE-2023/ GATE-2024/ GATE-2025) asthe case may be, conducted by respective NT/ MScin corresponding paperi.e. Electrical Engineering (EE), Mechanical Engineering (ME) and Civil Engineering (CE) shall only be eligible to be considered forselection.\nThe selection process consist of valid score of GATE (out of 1000) obtained in the corresponding paper of GATE-2023 / GATE-2024 / GATE-2025 score of GATE-2022 (as one time measure). No interview will be carried out for the posts being advertised by HPUs. The score of GATE- 2021 or priorwill not be entertained.\nThe applicant would require to fill up thevalid score of GATE (outof 1000) obtained in GATE-2023 / GATE-2024 / GATE-2025 or score of GATE- 2022 (as one time measure), whichever is higher during online submission of the application\nBesides this, Educational qualifications must be from a recognized Institution/ University/ Board.\nIn case the GATE score (out of 1000) of two or more candidates is equal then candidate older in age would be considered higher in merit. Further, in case age is also equal then candidate having more marks in essential qualification would be considered higherin merit.\nThe selected candidatesfor the post of Assistant Engineer will produce Medical Fitness certificate required for first entry into service from the Civil Surgeon of any district in Haryana State before joining the services.\nHow to Apply\nPlease read the instructions and procedures carefully before filling the online Application form. No request regarding any change against any entry in the online application form will be entertained once post applied,\nFor submission of online applications, candidates have to visit on website of HPUs i.e. www.hvpn.org.in. www.hpgcl.org.in. www.uhbvn.org.in & www.dhbvn.org.in\nThe application fees are to be paid online through electronic mode i.e. Debitcard/ Credit card/ Netbanking\nOnline application complete in all respects should be submitted within stipulated period starting from 29-09-2025 to 29-10-2025.\nThe application form received through Courier or any other means will not be entertained in any case and will be rejected. HARD Copy of online\nApplication form is not required to be submitted.\nIt is made clear that any delay in submission of online application form by the due date shall be sole responsibility of the candidate.\nThe candidate should retain printout of online application form alongwith application fee transaction for future reference and same will have to be brought by the candidates at the time of verification/ checking of the documents.\nOnline application that are incomplete and without prescribed fee will be rejected straightaway and no correspondence in this regard will be entertained\nCandidates are advised to apply online well in time without waiting for last date of submission of application.',285,'2025-09-29','2025-10-29','2025-09-29 11:28:53','https://hrpower.co.in/StaticPages/HomePage.aspx','https://dhbvn.org.in/staticContent/Advt+DH/Advt_GATE-2022-25_dt.25-09-2025.pdf',0),
(32,'National Institute of Electronics and Information Technology (NIELIT) Recruitment 2025 – Walk in for 07 Senior Resource Person, Junior Resource Person Posts','National Institute of Electronics and Information Technology (NIELIT)','UP','Full-time','','National Institute of Electronics and Information Technology (NIELIT) Recruitment 2025 for 07 posts of Senior Resource Person, Junior Resource Person. Candidates with BCA, B.Tech/B.E, CS, M.Sc, M.E/M.Tech, MS Can attend the walkin. The Walk-in on 08-10-2025. For detailed information please visit NIELIT official website, nielit.gov.in\n\nApplication Fee\n\nRegistration fee of Rs. 500/-\nNIELIT Recruitment 2025 Important Dates\n\nDate of Walkin Interview: 08-10-2025\n\nNIELIT Recruitment 2025 Age Limit\nNot Mentioned.\n\nQualification\n\nSr. Resource Person (S&T): M. Tech /M.E/MS (CS/IT)/C Level with 01 Year experience or B.E./B.TECH(CS/IT)/MCA/B-LEVEL with 02 years experience or M.Sc.(CS/IT) with 03 Year’s experience\nJr. Resource Person (S&T)- IT: B.E./B.TECH(CS/IT)/MCA/B-LEVEL or M.Sc(CS/IT) with 01 years experience or BCA/A-Level with 02 Years experience\nJr. Resource Person (Admin): Graduation with O Level/CCC Certificate.\n\nSalary\n\nSr. Resource Person (S&T): Rs.35000/-\nJr. Resource Person (S&T)- IT: Rs.-27500/-\nJr. Resource Person (Admin): Rs.- 24000/-\n\nNIELIT Recruitment 2025 Vacancy Details\nPost Name	Total\n\nSr. Resource Person (S&T)	02\nJr. Resource Person (S&T)- IT	03\nJr. Resource Person (Admin)	02',7,'2025-09-29','2025-10-08','2025-09-29 11:39:14','https://www.nielit.gov.in/gorakhpur/sites/default/files/Gorakhpur/Appliction%20Proforma%20Walk-in-Interview-_0.pdf','https://www.nielit.gov.in/gorakhpur/sites/default/files/Gorakhpur/14-Revised%20Details%20of%20Posts..pdf',0),
